WEBVTT

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:43.450
"Episode 22"
"Parade of Demise"

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:46.450
"Heavenly Gate Plaza, Rondacia Palace"

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:50.580
"Site of Prime Minister Golbarn's state funeral"

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:04.660
"Dorothea HQ"

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:08.040
Director, we're ready to depart.

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:09.410
Right.

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:13.450
Should we take the risk of
holding a state funeral now?

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:16.250
I have my doubts, to be honest.

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:18.040
Ray Dawn...

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:22.080
The acting prime minister must want
to set things in order quickly.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:24.700
In more ways than one, yes?

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:26.950
Yes.

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:28.370
Let's go.

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:32.500
Your Excellency, it is time.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:34.700
Right.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:38.370
Some are critical of holding a state funeral

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:41.410
when the prime minister's assassin
has not been identified,

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:44.000
but once the service is over,
I expect His Imperial Majesty

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.870
will formally appoint
Your Excellency as prime minister.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.830
Someone must govern this land.

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:56.330
If there is no one else suited
for the job, it will have to be me.

00:02:58.370 --> 00:03:02.080
The time has come. Time to settle things.

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:20.040
Okay.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:20.950
Let's go.

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:22.200
You got it.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:27.830
Director, Serge and Klara have gone on ahead.

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:30.250
As planned.

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:33.870
Do you suppose Veronica Thorn will show up?

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:38.450
We should be more vigilant
for the order than for her.

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:41.410
They desire a fairy-possessed.

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:42.620
Yes, ma'am.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:05.830
The order?!

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:22.370
Sure enough, they were
stockpiling artificial fairies.

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:23.580
Open fire!

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:29.580
Director!

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:32.160
We're now pivoting to
Operation Order Annihilation!

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:35.120
Guard the acting prime minister
as we modify our route!

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:36.000
Yes, ma'am!

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.040
Free!

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:38.080
Got it!

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:50.580
Anything?

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:53.120
No, nothing just yet.

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:00.750
A Fairy Soldier, in an alley!

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:02.160
Fairy Soldier...

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:03.580
Notify Free!

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:04.790
Okay!

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:10.200
Red... Fairy Soldier.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:11.910
Must be Wolfran.

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:13.290
Free.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:18.000
I'll be back.

00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:26.540
That's within range.

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:27.870
Go!

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:41.370
He repelled it?!

00:05:41.370 --> 00:05:44.000
Fratanil! It's a Fairy Weapon!

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:58.040
Serge.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:02.750
This was quick for you, Free.

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:10.540
Wolfran!

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:13.450
Free!

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:27.910
Why are you doing all this?!

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:30.120
You want to discuss it?

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:33.620
Answer me! Is it for your
dead wife and daughter?

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:35.910
What will be left once it's done?!

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:38.660
Nothing.

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:40.500
There'll be nothing left.

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:43.950
That's your answer?

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:48.160
Yeah, I'll finish you with my own two hands.

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:53.500
Come on! I'll stop you!

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:04.910
The order shouldn't have
much more they can throw at us.

00:07:04.910 --> 00:07:07.080
--Yeah.
--Yeah.

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:20.200
Shit!

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:32.500
You okay?

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:34.120
Yes, ma'am.

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:42.000
It can't be...!

00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:47.910
That guy?!

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:07.250
Beevee Liscar!

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:10.620
The curtain rises on a new conflict.

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:13.540
You feel it too, don't you, Ray Dawn?

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:18.450
You war-obsessed ghost!

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:28.410
I have to take you alive, but when the
Seven Knights fight each other...

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:30.040
...anything goes!

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:48.200
You don't seem old to me. Nice!

00:08:55.910 --> 00:09:00.620
Ghosts... should rest in the past!

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:08.950
Superb! This is it!

00:09:08.950 --> 00:09:10.790
This is the way!

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:32.500
Three of the Seven Knights, together!

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:35.080
What stage could be better!

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:37.250
Why are <i>you</i> with the order?!

00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:40.410
I fight, therefore I am.

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:44.120
If there's fighting here, I want in!

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:48.620
Insane as ever, I see!

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:50.580
Get the acting prime minister somewhere safe!

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:51.790
Yes, ma'am!

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:56.790
One makes his exit, eh?

00:09:56.790 --> 00:10:01.830
You go around disturbing society.
You're nothing but toxic!

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:04.830
I love fighting and freedom!

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:19.040
You can't match me...

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:25.580
...with a weapon like that!

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:27.000
Sophie!

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:36.200
What's the big idea?

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:40.450
Use it. I want to fight you on even terms.

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:42.450
Until I've had my fill.

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:53.330
You, at least, ought to die.

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:17.910
Are you all right?

00:11:17.910 --> 00:11:19.500
It isn't serious.

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:23.500
Dorothea HQ is meant to double
as an emergency refuge.

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:26.000
All right, Acting Prime Minister?

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:28.750
Chase! Marlya!

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:31.080
Klara!

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:35.040
Looks like HQ is out!
It's under attack by the order!

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:36.040
Robert!

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:40.080
Yeah, time for plan B.
We'll make for East End Base!

00:11:43.450 --> 00:11:44.620
Enemies!

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:54.950
We'll keep them busy! Go!

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:01.870
Acting Prime Minister...

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:07.370
Under these conditions,
it won't be easy to reach the base.

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:10.700
How about the witness protection hideout?

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:11.950
Yeah...

00:12:11.950 --> 00:12:13.700
That's our only choice now!

00:12:23.330 --> 00:12:25.700
Slowly. There we go.

00:12:29.830 --> 00:12:30.910
Robert.

00:12:30.910 --> 00:12:33.080
Yeah.

00:12:33.080 --> 00:12:35.500
How to proceed from here.

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:36.790
What do we do?

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:41.160
The acting prime minister's
injuries are pretty bad.

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:46.160
He probably has broken ribs, and maybe
an injured lung or something.

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:48.450
We have no way to treat him.

00:12:48.450 --> 00:12:52.750
If we just stay holed up here,
we'll be sitting ducks.

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:55.870
But we can't afford to move him around, either.

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:58.250
I'll try to find a way to
bring back medical help...

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:00.580
...and if possible, reinforcements.

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:02.250
Please do.

00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:07.750
Sorry. I wish I could stand guard,
but even if I was here...

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:14.500
Don't apologize. Having you
around is always a big help.

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:15.620
I'll hurry back.

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:16.830
All right.

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:46.450
Before we know it, we grow old, and weak.

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:54.080
I have no regrets.

00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:57.950
What good would those do now?

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:13.950
Ver!

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:17.950
If you're going to shoot me, do it now.

00:14:25.540 --> 00:14:26.750
Ver...

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:30.750
Veronica Thorn.

00:14:30.750 --> 00:14:35.040
Here you are, come to kill me...

00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:37.950
Ray Dawn!

00:14:37.950 --> 00:14:39.160
Stop!

00:14:41.250 --> 00:14:42.450
Marlya!

00:14:42.450 --> 00:14:43.790
Don't interfere!

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:51.370
If only it weren't for you...!

00:15:20.830 --> 00:15:22.750
To the bitter end, then!

00:15:23.870 --> 00:15:25.160
Ver!

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:37.620
Let's end it. All of it, with this.

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:41.080
I won't ask for forgiveness.

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:43.750
The fairy-possessed...

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:49.330
We shouldn't exist in the world of man.

00:15:49.330 --> 00:15:52.790
If only there had never been any fairies.

00:15:52.790 --> 00:16:01.410
Ancient things that just mislead people...
should be destroyed and burned away!

00:16:01.410 --> 00:16:05.910
That's why you tried to destroy
all of Suna, including us?

00:16:05.910 --> 00:16:11.870
If a man would kill another man,
he should dirty his own hands.

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:18.910
If he believes that way is right,
he shouldn't shy away from blood!

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:27.910
You don't regret what you've done.

00:16:27.910 --> 00:16:30.290
That's right.

00:16:30.290 --> 00:16:31.700
Truly?

00:16:33.160 --> 00:16:34.790
What a lie.

00:16:36.540 --> 00:16:41.200
This isn't the first time
Ver has tried to kill you.

00:16:46.330 --> 00:16:50.330
You arrested her, but then released her.

00:16:50.330 --> 00:16:52.660
Because she was still a child?

00:16:52.660 --> 00:16:56.910
You burned down Suna, and tried to kill us all.

00:16:56.910 --> 00:17:02.870
So if you believe in your cold heart that
was the right thing to do, then why?

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:06.450
He just took pity on me, that's all!

00:17:06.450 --> 00:17:08.950
That's not it.

00:17:08.950 --> 00:17:13.500
Isn't it... because you're regretful?

00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:16.750
I can't forgive what you did, either.

00:17:16.750 --> 00:17:21.000
But... But you didn't kill Ver.

00:17:22.870 --> 00:17:26.750
That's why I got to see her this way.

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:30.120
For that, I'm grateful.

00:17:30.120 --> 00:17:35.580
Grateful... To me?

00:17:38.250 --> 00:17:42.290
You should hate me.

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:50.500
Even if I offered you both my life,
it would likely never bring you cheer.

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:57.120
That's the nature of what I did.
That's how bad it was.

00:17:58.790 --> 00:18:00.540
Ray Dawn.

00:18:00.540 --> 00:18:03.040
I can't forgive your crime.

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:07.660
But hating you will only cause pain.

00:18:07.660 --> 00:18:10.950
There's nothing your death...

00:18:10.950 --> 00:18:14.660
Not a single thing it would resolve!

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:18.290
Ver...

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:24.580
The Suna forest was burned, but it did survive.

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:29.750
Even if things won't be like before,
it's possible to move forward.

00:18:29.750 --> 00:18:35.080
If I have nowhere to go, or no purpose
in life, I come up with something.

00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:37.000
You're not alone!

00:18:38.950 --> 00:18:40.500
Marlya...

00:18:48.370 --> 00:18:50.200
I'm sorry.

00:18:58.370 --> 00:19:00.750
It's fine if I'm not forgiven.

00:19:00.750 --> 00:19:03.500
I want to apologize, from the heart.

00:19:03.500 --> 00:19:06.450
I really am sorry!

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:14.750
But...

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:19.330
...if this is how it ends, I don't know what to do.

00:19:19.330 --> 00:19:23.000
I don't have any easy answers.

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:26.000
But let's put our heads together.

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:30.080
If you have nothing, you'll just
have to find something!

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:34.000
Everyone died, but I survived.

00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:37.750
Is it still okay for me to live a normal life?

00:19:37.750 --> 00:19:42.080
Of course it is! Your life is worth something.

00:19:42.080 --> 00:19:46.950
If you're safe and sound, that's enough for me.

00:19:55.580 --> 00:19:59.700
They had a safe house way out here.

00:19:59.700 --> 00:20:02.750
We only need one fairy-possessed.

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:04.410
The rest are in the way!

00:20:06.910 --> 00:20:08.700
No, not them!

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:27.000
Ray Dawn!

00:20:30.080 --> 00:20:38.200
This is a disappointing end for a hero, but,
it does make harvesting the element convenient.

00:20:44.040 --> 00:20:45.250
Marlya!

00:20:50.370 --> 00:20:52.160
Now then...

00:21:01.410 --> 00:21:05.160
This is not the end. It's the beginning.

00:22:35.870 --> 00:22:40.750
We respectfully supplicate the Original Fairy,
the progenitor of all things.

00:22:40.750 --> 00:22:44.790
For the ideal world to emerge.

00:22:44.790 --> 00:22:49.700
We respectfully supplicate the Original Fairy,
the progenitor of all things.

00:22:49.700 --> 00:22:51.370
For the ideal world to emerge.

00:22:51.370 --> 00:22:54.000
Archbishop.

00:22:54.000 --> 00:22:58.620
We respectfully supplicate the Original Fairy,
the progenitor of all things.

00:22:58.620 --> 00:23:10.330
Emerge and save us, o holy beast equal to God,
nearest to the Original Fairy!

00:23:10.330 --> 00:23:13.450
Together, with the ideal world.

00:23:39.200 --> 00:23:41.750
I will guide the people who survive.

00:23:41.750 --> 00:23:43.080
It's a meaningless battle!

00:23:43.080 --> 00:23:44.250
Why do you not kill me?

00:23:44.250 --> 00:23:45.540
We won't let it end!

00:23:45.540 --> 00:23:46.410
Marlya!

00:23:45.910 --> 00:23:48.410
"Next time"
"One from an Unending Dream"

00:23:46.410 --> 00:23:48.410
I will release the Divine Beast!
